# CI reviewer secrets for the jbaruch/coding-policy gh-aw PR review workflows.
# Set as GitHub Actions repository secrets:
#   https://github.com/jbaruch/hubitat-dev/settings/secrets/actions
# The Codex (OpenAI-family) reviewer reads CODEX_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY
# (CODEX_API_KEY wins when both are set). ANTHROPIC_API_KEY drives the Claude
# reviewer; TESSL_TOKEN authenticates the `tessl install` step for both.
# TESSL_TOKEN is also used by the CI workflow (.github/workflows/ci.yml) for the
# `tessl plugin lint` and changed-skills `tessl skill review` gate.
#
# Where to obtain each value:
#   CODEX_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY  OpenAI API key — https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY               Anthropic API key — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#   TESSL_TOKEN                     Tessl API key — https://tessl.io/account/api-keys
CODEX_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
TESSL_TOKEN=

# Runtime secret for the mcp-connector skill (skills/_scripts/hub_mcp.py) — NOT a CI secret,
# read from the local environment at call time:
#   HUBITAT_MCP_TOKEN  Bearer token for the hub's built-in AI (MCP) Connector Integration.
#                      Enable the app on the hub (Integrations -> Add Built-In Integration ->
#                      AI (MCP) Connector Integration) and copy the token from its app UI;
#                      reset it there if compromised. Local-network use only; never commit it.
#                      (hub_mcp.py also accepts --token-file as an alternative to this var.)
HUBITAT_MCP_TOKEN=
